      "title": "USGS Water Science School, Are raindrops shaped like teardrops?: popular culture draws teardrops; small raindrops (radius < 1 mm) are spherical, larger ones more like a hamburger bun; tug-of-war between surface tension and the air pressure pushing up against the bottom of the falling drop; fall velocity increases with size; larger than a radius of about 4.5 mm they become distorted like a parachute and break up into smaller drops",
